  "request": {
    "spec": "A claim now belongs to the period containing its due-by date, not its date (the due-by as fixed at\ncreation; for a claim about to be added, its date plus the terms it would get). Everything that\ndepends on a claim's period follows: the period shown on the claim, period totals and the per-person\nperiod figures, per-period numbering, which claims a soft-closed period takes as late entries (by\nthe due-by the claim would be fixed with), and which claims a closed period refuses (a claim whose\ndue-by falls in a closed period cannot be added, edited, opened, settled or voided; a claim dated in\na closed period whose due-by falls outside it can).\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nA claim now belongs to the period containing its due-by date, not its date (the due-by as fixed at\ncreation; for a claim about to be added, its date plus the terms it would get). Everything that\ndepends on a claim's period follows: the period shown on the claim, period totals and the per-person\nperiod figures, per-period numbering, which claims a soft-closed period takes as late entries (by\nthe due-by the claim would be fixed with), and which claims a closed period refuses (a claim whose\ndue-by falls in a closed period cannot be added, edited, opened, settled or voided; a claim dated in\na closed period whose due-by falls outside it can).\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
